Emit a stub Cargo.toml when root_src is None.

Some crate_universe-generated rust_library targets expose CrateInfo with
.root == None (e.g. workspace-only crates that re-export deps — zenoh-
collections, zenoh-result). The aspect would crash at the `root_src.path`
deref in the template. Returning [] early leaves the declared manifest
file with no generating action (downstream aspect consumers still expect
it to exist). Write a stub Cargo.toml and return the normal providers.

--- a/cbindgen/cargo_manifest.bzl
+++ b/cbindgen/cargo_manifest.bzl
@@ -274,3 +274,18 @@ def _cargo_manifest_aspect_impl(target, ctx):
         root_src = _find_crate_root_from_srcs(src_files)
         if not root_src:
             fail("Could not find crate root (lib.rs or main.rs) in srcs for {}".format(target.label))
+
+    # Some crate_universe rust_library targets expose CrateInfo with .root
+    # == None (workspace-only crates that re-export deps, e.g.
+    # zenoh-collections, zenoh-result). Write a stub Cargo.toml so the
+    # already-declared `manifest` output has a generating action and
+    # downstream aspect consumers still see CargoManifestInfo on this dep.
+    if not root_src:
+        ctx.actions.write(
+            output = manifest,
+            content = "# stub manifest: {} has no crate root\n".format(target.label),
+        )
+        return [
+            CargoManifestInfo(toml = manifest, deps = depset()),
+            OutputGroupInfo(all_files = depset([manifest])),
+        ]
